NAME=node
VERSION=22.22.3
DESCRIPTION="Static Node.js 22 LTS runtime (jitless V8, small-icu, bundled deps, +npm)"
CATEGORY=lang
DEPS=
URL=https://nodejs.org/dist/v22.22.3/node-v22.22.3.tar.xz
SHA256=f3e6a578db1ab335a4a72785c1e87ad18a2cf6d2fc25747a1d741fb34af0bd0f
MAINTAINER=m3os

# Phase 89 — Node.js is the FOURTH cross-compiled language runtime on the Phase
# 85a `.m3pkg` substrate (after 85c Python, 85d Clang, 86d Go) and the heaviest
# managed runtime in the tree (V8 JIT engine + libuv async I/O + bundled
# OpenSSL/ICU/c-ares/nghttp2/llhttp/brotli). It is fully **static** — m3OS's
# custom `ld-musl` has no real `libc.so`, so `--fully-static` (no PT_INTERP,
# `dlopen` disabled) is the same loaderless contract as static CPython/Go/Clang.
#
# Toolchain note — LIKE llvm (not the musl-gcc C-port path): Node is C++17/20 and
# `musl-tools` ships no C++ compiler, so `build_node` (xtask/src/port_build.rs)
# drives the host **clang/clang++** as the cross-compiler
# (`--target=x86_64-unknown-linux-musl` + the assembled musl sysroot + the
# `build_llvm` Stage-B static `libc++.a`), with host glibc clang for the
# `*_host` toolset (V8's `mksnapshot`/`torque` run natively on the build host —
# same arch x86_64 — which is the one thing that makes a Node cross-build
# tractable). DEPS is empty: every dependency is vendored into the static binary.
#
# V8 / W^X model — the crux of the phase. m3OS forbids `PROT_WRITE|PROT_EXEC`
# (W^X; the green `wx-violation` gate). Modern V8 REMOVED the old `mprotect`
# RW↔RX "write-protected code memory" JIT mechanism; it is now PKU-or-RWX,
# neither of which m3OS allows. So this port ships jitless V8 via
# **`--v8-options=--jitless`** as the PRIMARY supported config: V8 allocates ZERO
# runtime executable memory (all JS runs through the Ignition interpreter;
# builtins are embedded RX in the binary's `.text` by the normal ELF loader), so
# it never requests an `mprotect(W|X)` mapping. (NOT `--v8-lite-mode`: that also
# compiles WASM OUT, but Node 22 unconditionally passes default
# `--experimental-wasm-*` V8 flags at startup that a WASM-less V8 rejects as a
# fatal "bad option" before `node --version` prints; keeping WASM compiled in +
# `--jitless` makes node start cleanly while staying W^X-safe.) PKU-backed JIT is
# a tracked follow-up (needs a kernel MPK/`pkey_mprotect` story). See build_node
# in xtask/src/port_build.rs and docs/89-nodejs.md for the full recipe + non-goals.
#
# Intl — `--with-intl=small-icu` (en-US bundled; `Intl`/`Intl.NumberFormat`
# work, artifact stays lean). npm/npx are kept (bundled JS in lib/node_modules).
